        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Postpartum Depression (PPD) Screening Test",
        "text_sha256": "0da7852ed9652d8f25359bec27dce84e822504b899f6b40dbbf154763fb1ca64",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "PPD screening tool",
        "text_sha256": "65ca2496b45ea6744163ba77e1535ee24554e7aaa95f47de0cc9c180e8630385",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "This postpartum screening test is based off the Edinburgh Postnatal Depression Scale (EPDS) and can help you check for common symptoms of PPD.",
        "text_sha256": "b8dd572e999092be31b9d6d5cfb92e5eda80765910979aed591d7247b779ed6f",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "It’s normal to have mixed feelings about becoming a parent. You may be excited to get to know your newborn, but also overwhelmed, irritable, sad or anxious (or all of the above). Sometimes, these “baby blues” linger and grow worse, developing into a more serious condition called postpartum depression (PPD).",
        "text_sha256": "fd8015223994c23a7ee6e026cae2a5c63e474836f76b436211d96702721af2cc",
        "word_count": 50
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "This depression screening test, which is based off the Edinburgh Postnatal Depression Scale (EPDS), may help you determine whether you’re experiencing symptoms of PPD. The test is free and your results are confidential. This is not an official diagnosis, and regardless of your score, you should call your health care provider if something doesn’t seem right.",
        "text_sha256": "6dfbe666015370584c513ccba5d1bf78ce62aab9a8b9c81e578f3c6aae1db735",
        "word_count": 56
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Always remember that if you're diagnosed with PPD or another perinatal mood and anxiety disorder , you're not alone, it's never your fault and help is available.",
        "text_sha256": "920b127e952e26718f4a2c11a3126af0b5bc89caeae0231a5faec2660881d141",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "blockquote",
        "tag": "blockquote",
        "text": "What to Expect the First Year , 3rd edition, Heidi Murkoff. WhatToExpect.com, Postpartum Depression , April 2021. WhatToExpect.com, The Baby Blues , April 2021. WhatToExpect.com, Postpartum Anxiety , April 2021. WhatToExpect.com, Postpartum PTSD , April 2021. The American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists, Postpartum Depression , November 2019. Mayo Clinic, Postpartum Depression , September 2018. Adapted from the Edinburgh Postnatal Depression Scale (EPDS).",
        "text_sha256": "20968d1cc609868740e62aafba9272f0a4d17d59a8204587a6e06b05ed82f119",
        "word_count": 63
      },
      {
